# q12-rotation.script — Q12 event-parity fixture: 'e'/'r' press-then-release
#
# D16 rows exercised (see test/harness/d16-state-machine.md):
#   - KeyDown 'e'/'r': sets AngularVelocity (+thrust coupling); sets the
#     pending-rotation flag ONLY when already rotating the other way.
#   - KeyUp 'e'/'r': CONSUMES the pending flag and zeroes/flips angular
#     velocity. This is the release-consumption semantics a per-frame
#     boolean key-state array cannot express (the B3 regression test).
#   - Phase 2 holds 'e', taps 'r' (pending flag arms), releases 'e':
#     velocity must FLIP to rightward, not stop.
#
# Pass criteria (Q12): identical object state at every checkpoint when this
# script runs on X11 vs GL/VK (positions/velocities/state hashes) — NOT a
# pixel diff against qa/baseline-x11. No repeat-delivery divergence: exactly
# ONE velocity transition per press, none per repeat.
#
# Run:
#   ./obj/harness --seed 12345 --script test/harness/scripts/q12-rotation.script \
#       --out DIR --hiscore test/harness/fixtures/hiScore.nul.data
# (GL/VK legs add their own --ref pairing per task 31/42; gameplay seq values
# below are conservative starting points — pin them empirically per
# script-format.md authoring rule 3 before first use.)

1    capture q12_help       # initial static screen

3    keydown s              # start game
6    keyup s
40   capture q12_start      # ship idle, pre-input

# --- phase 1: hold left rotation, release zeroes it
50   keydown e
54   capture q12_e_held     # rotating left
62   keyup e
70   capture q12_e_released # velocity zeroed by release consumption

# --- phase 2: pending-flag flip (hold 'e', tap 'r', release 'e')
80   keydown e
88   keydown r              # arms rightRotPending (still rotating left)
92   keyup r                # no-op on velocity ('r' release with AV<0)
100  keyup e                # consumes pending flag -> velocity flips right
110  capture q12_flip       # rotating RIGHT without any held key

130  keydown q
134  keyup q
